meta {
  name: Update Item
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Updated title",
    "parentId": "{{parentItemId}}",
    "isAttached": true
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Item

  Title, description and assignment, plus `parentId` and `isAttached`, which
  run the same hierarchy rules as `PATCH /api/items/{id}/move` (see Move
  Item). `workphaseId` and placement aren't accepted here. `parentId` and
  `agentId` take an id, or `null` for none: an empty string names no row, and
  is a 400.

  A write that omits `isAttached` keeps the item's state, so reparenting a
  top-level item makes it a detached child: send `isAttached: true` to
  attach it. `isAttached: true` without a parent is a 400.

  See wiki item-attachment §1, §2a, §4.
}
